/*
| Setup catalogue (HROne parity): one place per module where a client's administrator configures PeopleOS, like
| HROne's Setup. Each module lists
|   settings      typed tenant settings (SettingsRepository keys) the module reads, with label, help and validation;
|   policy_types  Policy Engine types (config peopleos.policies.types) that drive the module per employee group;
|   links         the module's masters and configuration screens (Filament resource or page classes; a link the
|                 viewer cannot open is not shown).
| A setting is listed only when code reads it: nothing here is configuration without effect. Defaults live in
| peopleos.settings; a tenant row overrides them.
|
| Setting types: boolean, number, text, textarea, select (options or options_from), multiselect (options or options_from), roles,
| date (a select may be `nullable`: blank allowed; a text may carry a `pattern`), matrix (rows × boolean columns, stored as {row: {column: bool}}; `rows` or `rows_from` a config list, `columns`) and
| file (an image or document on the documents disk; `accept` image|document, `max_kb`; `public` lets every signed-in person of
| the organisation fetch it, e.g. the logo, otherwise settings.view; every fetch goes through SettingFiles, signed and audited).
| A setting may carry a `group` (a heading such as HROne's Expense / Travel / Exceptional expense): a module whose settings
| are grouped shows one block per group.
*/

